7. Conclusion
Causality assessment is an important component of pharmacovigilance because it helps determine the likelihood that a drug caused an adverse reaction. The assessment should consider the time relationship, dechallenge, rechallenge, known drug reactions, and alternative causes.
In the case studies:
Amoxicillin → Skin rash → Certain
Ibuprofen → Gastric irritation → Probable
Metformin → Nausea → Possible
Causality assessment should be based on the available clinical information and should not assume that every adverse event occurring during drug treatment was necessarily caused by the drug.